-- json.talk: decoding and encoding JSON with the `json` Library (ADR 0021).
-- The Host granted `http` (suspending) and `log`.

use decodeJson, encodeJson from json

on fetchStation url
  ask http to get url and wait
  put decodeJson(the body of it as text) into data
  -- Was: put the json of (raw as text) into data
  -- `json` is a Library written in the language, so its Fuel comes from its
  -- instructions, the same on both Cores. Invalid JSON raises `can't decode`
  -- with {format: "json", at: …}.

  -- {"station": "LHR", "gust_kph": null, "temp_c": 11.20}
  --   `null` decodes to Nothing, which may sit inside a map or list.
  --   `11.20` decodes through `as number`, so the trailing zero survives.
  if the gust_kph of data is nothing then tell log to write "no gust reading"

  -- Encoding keeps insertion order and writes decimals in canonical form.
  tell log to write encodeJson({station: "LHR", temp: 11.20, gust: nothing})
  -- → {"station":"LHR","temp":11.20,"gust":null}

  -- Kinds with no JSON form must be converted first:
  --   encodeJson({wind: 14 km/hr})          -- raises `wrong kind`
  --   encodeJson({wind: (14 km/hr) as text}) -- "14 km/hr"
  -- ?? Or should Quantities encode as {"value": 14, "unit": "km/hr"}? ADR 0021
  --    says convert first. One spec section governs the mapping for the
  --    Library and the Host's JSON ↔ Value codec alike.
end fetchStation
